    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189-a3">

                <pb facs="0279" n="173" xml:id="pg173"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 205.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Señor Matta</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic">September 26,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I nave the honor to refer to my note of
                    yesterday’s date addressed to your excellency, and now beg to inclose copy of a
                    letter which I have just received from a citizen of the United States, Mr. W. E.
                    Ray craft, giving particulars of the manlier in which he was treated by the
                    police, when on yesterday he attempted to enter this legation to inquire for his
                    correspondence.</p>
                <p>With sentiments, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Patrick Egan</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
